+Local scaling and Weber convention
+----------------------------------
+q=sqrt(epsilon), y=-1+qX,
+e=-3/2+q^2 e1+q^4 e2+..., and s=3^(1/4)X.  The exact scaled
+coefficient through q^2 is
+
+R=3X^2+2(e1+1-delta)
+ +q[10X^3+(4e1+6-6delta)X]
+ +q^2[22X^4+(6e1+12-12delta)X^2+delta^2-delta+2e2]+O(q^3).
+
+The DLMF convention is D_nu(Z)=U(-nu-1/2,Z), so
+D_nu(sqrt(2)s) solves u_ss=[s^2-(2nu+1)]u.
+
+Candidate sector pairs and energy branches
+------------------------------------------
+- Opposite sectors centred on the real s axis:
+  e1=delta-1-sqrt(3)(n+1/2).
+- Opposite sectors centred on the imaginary s axis, t=-is:
+  e1=delta-1+sqrt(3)(n+1/2).
+- Adjacent-sector formulae do not give a third integer branch.
+
+The Stage 09b geometry does not select the physical pair.  The assertion
+that the imaginary-axis pair is selected is named the Fedoryuk--Bargmann
+orientation hypothesis.  Its agreement with Stage 08/Bogoliubov is only an
+independent consistency check.
+
+Local wavefunctions and pullback
+--------------------------------
+phi_n(w)=pi^(-1/4)(2^n n!)^(-1/2) exp(-w^2/2) H_n(w).
+The leading local solutions are phi_n(s) and phi_n(-is).  Since exactly
+X=z+eta^(1/3), their sectorial pullbacks are
+
+Psi_loc,R=z^(-delta) exp(eta/z) phi_n(3^(1/4)[z+eta^(1/3)]),
+Psi_loc,I=z^(-delta) exp(eta/z) phi_n(-i3^(1/4)[z+eta^(1/3)]).
+
+The logarithm, sector, and local normalization are fixed.  No global
+Bargmann regularity or normalization is claimed.
+
+First correction
+----------------
+An explicit intermediate-normalized local u1 was obtained.  The odd
+cubic-plus-linear perturbation couples only n+-1 and n+-3.  Its diagonal
+matrix element vanishes, so there is no q-order energy correction.  The
+rotated branch uses the analytically continued contour bilinear form; no
+real-axis L2 argument is silently imported.
